<title>UK: L-Bank sets $250 million six-year bond. [CORRECTED 15:30 GMT]</title>
<headline>L-Bank sets $250 million six-year bond. [CORRECTED 15:30 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced</p>
<p>by joint lead managers Merrill Lynch and DKB International (corrects from Dresdner Kleinwort Benson).</p>
<p> BORROWER   LANDESKREDITBANK BADEN-WUERTTEMBOERG</p>
<p> AMT    $250 MLN	COUPON     6.0	 MATURITY    12.DEC.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.0     PAY DATE    12.DEC.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.875     REOFFER    99.40     SPREAD	+12 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LONDON    PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK/GE</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   MGT/UND    0.275     SELL CONC  1.60</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF AN EMTN PROGRAMME.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
